Sogen: the analyzer runs child processes on KVM too

The analyzer gave a guest a process manager only on the WHP backend;
on any other, NtCreateUserProcess answered STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED. The
manager runs each child in a sandbox process of its own, and the
sandbox builds with WHP on Windows and KVM on Linux: the sandbox tool
itself runs child processes on KVM through the same manager.

nodecode's platform seams run a shell and a detached cmd as children;
under the KVM backend neither could start.

The analyzer now makes the manager on KVM as well; the sandbox
executable has to sit beside it, as it does for WHP.

